From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Asius <dev@asius.ai>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 10:45:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ufs: qcom: enable device temperature notifications

Qualcomm UFS controllers can use the core query path for UFS 3.0 device
temperature attributes and exception events. Advertise that capability so
devices which report high/low temperature notification support get the UFS
hwmon interface.

Signed-off-by: Asius <dev@asius.ai>
---
 drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
index 7c5fcbb0241f..4022d1009da8 100644
--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
@@ -1165,6 +1165,7 @@ static void ufs_qcom_set_caps(struct ufs_hba *hba)
 	hba->caps |= UFSHCD_CAP_WB_EN;
 	hba->caps |= UFSHCD_CAP_AGGR_POWER_COLLAPSE;
 	hba->caps |= UFSHCD_CAP_RPM_AUTOSUSPEND;
+	hba->caps |= UFSHCD_CAP_TEMP_NOTIF;
 
 	ufs_qcom_set_host_caps(hba);
 }
-- 
